  "title": "Copán",
  "summary": "Copán, in western Honduras, was a Classic Maya city whose dynasty began with K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo' in 426 CE and ended with the city's abandonment in the early tenth century. Its Great Plaza, Acropolis, ball court and Hieroglyphic Stairway, with the longest known Maya inscription, make it a UNESCO site, listed in 1980.",
